1872:     /**
1873:      * This method signals the background thread to {@link CreateFetchRequestsEvent create fetch requests}.
1874:      *
1875:      * <p/>
1876:      *
1877:      * This method takes the following steps to maintain compatibility with the {@link ClassicKafkaConsumer} method
1878:      * of the same name:
1879:      *
1880:      * <ul>
1881:      *     <li>
1882:      *         The method will wait for confirmation of the request creation before continuing.
1883:      *     </li>
1884:      *     <li>
1885:      *         The method will throw exceptions encountered during request creation to the user <b>immediately</b>.
1886:      *     </li>
1887:      *     <li>
1888:      *         The method will suppress {@link TimeoutException}s that occur while waiting for the confirmation.
1889:      *         Timeouts during request creation are a byproduct of this consumer's thread communication mechanisms.
1890:      *         That exception type isn't thrown in the request creation step of the {@link ClassicKafkaConsumer}.
1891:      *         Additionally, timeouts will not impact the logic of {@link #pollForFetches(Timer) blocking requests}
1892:      *         as it can handle requests that are created after the timeout.
1893:      *     </li>
