1396:     /**
1397:      * Please keep these tenets in mind for the implementation of the {@link AsyncKafkaConsumer}’s
1398:      * {@link #close(Duration)} method. In the future, these tenets may be made officially part of the top-level
1399:      * {@link KafkaConsumer#close(Duration)} API, but for now they remain here.
1400:      *
1401:      * <ol>
1402:      *     <li>
1403:      *         The execution of the {@link ConsumerRebalanceListener} callback (if applicable) must be performed on
1404:      *         the application thread to ensure it does not interfere with the network I/O on the background thread.
1405:      *     </li>
1406:      *     <li>
1407:      *         The {@link ConsumerRebalanceListener} callback execution must complete before an attempt to leave
1408:      *         the consumer group is performed. In this context, “complete” does not necessarily imply
1409:      *         <em>success</em>; execution is “complete” even if the execution <em>fails</em> with an error.
1410:      *     </li>
1411:      *     <li>
1412:      *         Any error thrown during the {@link ConsumerRebalanceListener} callback execution will be caught to
1413:      *         ensure it does not prevent execution of the remaining {@link #close()} logic.
1414:      *     </li>
1415:      *     <li>
1416:      *         The application thread will be blocked during the entire duration of the execution of the
1417:      *         {@link ConsumerRebalanceListener}. The consumer does not employ a mechanism to short-circuit the
1418:      *         callback execution, so execution is not bound by the timeout in {@link #close(Duration)}.
1419:      *     </li>
1420:      *     <li>
1421:      *         A given {@link ConsumerRebalanceListener} implementation may be affected by the application thread's
1422:      *         interrupt state. If the callback implementation performs any blocking operations, it may result in
1423:      *         an error. An implementation may choose to preemptively check the thread's interrupt flag via
1424:      *         {@link Thread#isInterrupted()} or {@link Thread#isInterrupted()} and alter its behavior.
1425:      *     </li>
1426:      *     <li>
1427:      *         If the application thread was interrupted <em>prior</em> to the execution of the
1428:      *         {@link ConsumerRebalanceListener} callback, the thread's interrupt state will be preserved for the
1429:      *         {@link ConsumerRebalanceListener} execution.
1430:      *     </li>
1431:      *     <li>
1432:      *         If the application thread was interrupted <em>prior</em> to the execution of the
1433:      *         {@link ConsumerRebalanceListener} callback <em>but</em> the callback cleared out the interrupt state,
1434:      *         the {@link #close()} method will not make any effort to restore the application thread's interrupt
1435:      *         state for the remainder of the execution of {@link #close()}.
1436:      *     </li>
1437:      *     <li>
1438:      *         Leaving the consumer group is achieved by issuing a ‘leave group‘ network request. The consumer will
1439:      *         attempt to leave the group on a “best-case” basis. There is no stated guarantee that the consumer will
1440:      *         have successfully left the group before the {@link #close()} method completes processing.
1441:      *     </li>
1442:      *     <li>
1443:      *         The consumer will attempt to leave the group regardless of the timeout elapsing or the application
1444:      *         thread receiving an {@link InterruptException} or {@link InterruptedException}.
1445:      *     </li>
1446:      *     <li>
1447:      *         The application thread will wait for confirmation that the consumer left the group until one of the
1448:      *         following occurs:
1449:      *
1450:      *         <ol>
1451:      *             <li>Confirmation that the ’leave group‘ response was received from the group coordinator</li>
1452:      *             <li>The timeout provided by the user elapses</li>
1453:      *             <li>An {@link InterruptException} or {@link InterruptedException} is thrown</li>
1454:      *         </ol>
1455:      *     </li>
1456:      * </ol>
1457:      */
1458:     private void close(Duration timeout, CloseOptions.GroupMembershipOperation membershipOperation, boolean swallowException) {
1459:         log.trace("Closing the Kafka consumer");
1460:         AtomicReference<Throwable> firstException = new AtomicReference<>();
1461: 
1462:         // We are already closing with a timeout, don't allow wake-ups from here on.
1463:         wakeupTrigger.disableWakeups();
1464: 
1465:         final Timer closeTimer = createTimerForCloseRequests(timeout);
1466:         clientTelemetryReporter.ifPresent(ClientTelemetryReporter::initiateClose);
1467:         closeTimer.update();
1468:         // Prepare shutting down the network thread
1469:         // Prior to closing the network thread, we need to make sure the following operations happen in the right
1470:         // sequence...
1471:         swallow(log, Level.ERROR, "Failed to auto-commit offsets",
1472:             () -> autoCommitOnClose(closeTimer), firstException);
1473:         swallow(log, Level.ERROR, "Failed to stop finding coordinator",
1474:             this::stopFindCoordinatorOnClose, firstException);
1475:         swallow(log, Level.ERROR, "Failed to release group assignment",
1476:             this::runRebalanceCallbacksOnClose, firstException);
1477:         swallow(log, Level.ERROR, "Failed to leave group while closing consumer",
1478:             () -> leaveGroupOnClose(closeTimer, membershipOperation), firstException);
1479:         swallow(log, Level.ERROR, "Failed invoking asynchronous commit callbacks while closing consumer",
1480:             () -> awaitPendingAsyncCommitsAndExecuteCommitCallbacks(closeTimer, false), firstException);
1481:         if (applicationEventHandler != null)
1482:             closeQuietly(() -> applicationEventHandler.close(Duration.ofMillis(closeTimer.remainingMs())), "Failed shutting down network thread", firstException);
1483:         closeTimer.update();
1484: 
1485:         // close() can be called from inside one of the constructors. In that case, it's possible that neither
1486:         // the reaper nor the background event queue were constructed, so check them first to avoid NPE.
1487:         if (backgroundEventReaper != null && backgroundEventQueue != null)
1488:             backgroundEventReaper.reap(backgroundEventQueue);
1489: 
1490:         closeQuietly(interceptors, "consumer interceptors", firstException);
1491:         closeQuietly(kafkaConsumerMetrics, "kafka consumer metrics", firstException);
1492:         closeQuietly(metrics, "consumer metrics", firstException);
1493:         closeQuietly(deserializers, "consumer deserializers", firstException);
1494:         clientTelemetryReporter.ifPresent(reporter -> closeQuietly(reporter, "async consumer telemetry reporter", firstException));
1495: 
1496:         AppInfoParser.unregisterAppInfo(CONSUMER_JMX_PREFIX, clientId, metrics);
1497:         log.debug("Kafka consumer has been closed");
1498:         Throwable exception = firstException.get();
1499:         if (exception != null && !swallowException) {
1500:             if (exception instanceof InterruptException) {
1501:                 throw (InterruptException) exception;
1502:             }
1503:             throw new KafkaException("Failed to close kafka consumer", exception);
1504:         }
1505:     }
