2151:     /**
2152:      * This method can be used by cases where the caller has an event that needs to both block for completion but
2153:      * also process background events. For some events, in order to fully process the associated logic, the
2154:      * {@link ConsumerNetworkThread background thread} needs assistance from the application thread to complete.
2155:      * If the application thread simply blocked on the event after submitting it, the processing would deadlock.
2156:      * The logic herein is basically a loop that performs two tasks in each iteration:
2157:      *
2158:      * <ol>
2159:      *     <li>Process background events, if any</li>
2160:      *     <li><em>Briefly</em> wait for {@link CompletableApplicationEvent an event} to complete</li>
2161:      * </ol>
2162:      *
2163:      * <p/>
2164:      *
2165:      * Each iteration gives the application thread an opportunity to process background events, which may be
